# tools/hunk_edit_cursor_witness.rish — the Photos app undo/redo cursor on metal (HUNK16).
#
# Season A (Hardware & Right-to-Repair) · waymark HUNK · journey Photos app · rung HUNK16.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260813/20260813-171500_hunk-edit-cursor-undo-redo-exploration.md.
# Teacher, thanked clean-room: the undo/redo history stack of a photo editor (iCloud Photos / Google Photos) — a
# position walks a recorded history, and a fresh edit past a rewind discards the branch not kept (concept only, siloed).
#
# HUNK11 recorded the six Photos verbs as a bounded edit-list and replayed them over an untouched source; HUNK14 made a
# revert dropping edits off the end. This rung holds the piece redo actually needs: an `EditCursor` carries the whole
# reachable history plus a `position`. Undo steps back, redo steps forward, and the image a keeper sees is the first
# `position` edits replayed — a walk destroys nothing, so ten undos roll forward again byte-for-byte. The one new law:
# a fresh push while rewound forgets the redo tail. The selftest proves the walk both ways byte-for-byte, that a
# rewind-then-push forgets the discarded verb, that undo/redo clamp at both edges, that the applied prefix still
# round-trips as an open record, and that the edit ceiling still refuses. No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/hunk_edit_cursor_witness.rish

say "hunk-edit-cursor: Language EN — HUNK16 carries a position over the recorded history; undo steps back, redo steps forward, and the viewed image is the first position edits replayed."
say "hunk-edit-cursor: Style Radiant — a walk destroys nothing, so every undo rolls forward again; only a fresh edit ever forgets a road, and only the road left behind."
say "hunk-edit-cursor: Lens TAME — the cursor is one edit-list plus a u32 with the invariant position <= count; undo/redo clamp without under/overflow; no new storage, no new error; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/edit_cursor"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/edit_cursor.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "hunk-edit-cursor: build failed — ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "hunk-edit-cursor: selftest exited non-zero — ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "hunk-edit-cursor: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-edit-cursor" else "hunk-edit-cursor: selftest did not print the GREEN cursor line"

assert selftest.out contains "redo returns to the full image byte-for-byte" else "hunk-edit-cursor: undo/redo did not walk the history byte-for-byte"

assert selftest.out contains "every step rolls forward again unchanged" else "hunk-edit-cursor: a full rewind did not roll forward again unchanged"

assert selftest.out contains "forgets the redo tail" else "hunk-edit-cursor: a fresh edit while rewound did not forget the redo tail"

assert selftest.out contains "clamp at both edges without" else "hunk-edit-cursor: undo/redo did not clamp at both edges"

assert selftest.out contains "still round-trips as an open fixed-point record" else "hunk-edit-cursor: the applied prefix did not round-trip as an open record"

say "hunk-edit-cursor: GREEN — the Photos app walks its history: undo and redo byte-for-byte, a fresh edit forgets the road not taken, both edges clamped, the applied prefix still an open record; no network, no key, no funds."
